{
  "title": "Epididymitis: follow the site and route",
  "sources": [
    "CH24S44",
    "CH24S45",
    "CH26S31",
    "CH26S28"
  ],
  "stages": [
    {
      "start": 0,
      "title": "Locate the structures",
      "text": "Locate the testis, epididymis, and vas deferens on the anatomical illustration. The testis produces sperm. Sperm mature in the epididymis, and the vas deferens transports them toward the urethra."
    },
    {
      "start": 12.78,
      "title": "Follow the infection route",
      "text": "For epididymitis, reverse that usual direction. The supplied slide describes a microorganism ascending the vas deferens from an infected bladder or urethra to reach the epididymis. Watch the highlighted inflammatory change develop at the epididymis."
    },
    {
      "start": 27.64,
      "title": "Distinguish the affected organ",
      "text": "Epididymitis is inflammation of the epididymis. Orchitis is infection of the testis and may occur with epididymitis. Similar pain does not make these the same affected structure."
    },
    {
      "start": 39.16,
      "title": "Study within the source limits",
      "text": "The epididymitis slide lists pain and the Prehn sign, with antibiotics, analgesics, ice, and scrotal elevation as treatments. It does not provide a complete organism or complication list. Those textbook details remain marked as gaps in this guide."
    }
  ],
